1
00:00:00,927 --> 00:00:05,767
(Leonard:)...which clearly appears to be a previously
unknown state of matter.

2
00:00:05,932 --> 00:00:07,812
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

3
00:00:07,976 --> 00:00:09,556
(Leonard:)Thank you.

4
00:00:14,148 --> 00:00:15,938
- Are there any questions?
MAN: Yeah.

5
00:00:16,401 --> 00:00:18,651
(Voice:)What the hell was that?

6
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:21,990
(Leonard:)Any other questions?

7
00:00:22,532 --> 00:00:26,702
Dr. Sheldon Cooper here.
I am the lead author of this particular paper.

8
00:00:28,746 --> 00:00:30,416
(Leonard:)Thank you.

9
00:00:31,457 --> 00:00:34,127
(Sheldon(who previously spoke, now removing his hood and dark glasses):)And you, sir, you have completely
skipped over the part...

10
00:00:34,294 --> 00:00:36,214
(Sheldon(who previously spoke, now removing his hood and dark glasses):)...where I was walking through
the park...

11
00:00:36,379 --> 00:00:38,629
(Sheldon(who previously spoke, now removing his hood and dark glasses):)...and I saw these children
on a merry-go-round...

12
00:00:38,798 --> 00:00:41,508
(Sheldon(who previously spoke, now removing his hood and dark glasses):)...which started me thinking
about the moment of inertia...

13
00:00:41,676 --> 00:00:44,766
(Sheldon(who previously spoke, now removing his hood and dark glasses):)...in gasses like helium at temperatures
approaching absolute zero.

14
00:00:44,929 --> 00:00:47,599
(Leonard:)I didn't skip it.
It's just an anecdote. It's not science.

15
00:00:47,765 --> 00:00:50,765
Oh, I see. It was the apple falling
on Newton's head.

16
00:00:50,935 --> 00:00:52,185
(Sheldon:)Was that just an anecdote?

17
00:00:52,353 --> 00:00:54,563
- You are not Isaac Newton.
- No, no, that's true.

18
00:00:54,731 --> 00:00:57,481
(Sheldon:)Gravity would have been apparent to me
without the apple.

19
00:00:57,650 --> 00:00:59,230
You cannot be that arrogant.

